# Arcade Integration Rules

- `@arcadeai/arcadejs` is imported ONLY from `lib/arcade/**`. Anywhere else
  must go through the typed wrappers in `lib/arcade/tools.ts`.
- The Arcade client is a singleton — instantiate it once via
  `lib/arcade/client.ts` and reuse.
- Every call to `client.tools.execute` MUST pass an explicit `user_id`. The
  `user_id` MUST equal the `approved_by` field on the parent intent —
  enforced by `lib/aig/executor.ts` and surfaced as `AIGBlockedAuthError`
  when violated.
- Use `client.tools.formatted.list({ format: 'anthropic', toolkit })` to
  fetch tool definitions for Claude. Do not hand-wrap tool schemas.
- Never log API keys. Pino is configured to redact `ARCADE_API_KEY` and any
  field matching `*.apiKey`.
- The mock Arcade client (`lib/arcade/mock.ts`, used when
  `E2E_MOCK_ARCADE=1`) MUST match the real client's type surface exactly
  so the executor cannot tell them apart at the type level.
